WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.560
Since ancient times,

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.480
the stars have captured mankind's imagination and garnered its respect.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.360
The twinkling seen from earth,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.690
the shine seen from a spaceship...

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.030
Different times and different distances,

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.230
but the effect on the human heart is the same.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.740
Even in an era when space is freely traversed,

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.300
the beauty of the stars

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.040
amidst the night sky never fades.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.540
Welcome to Calmwind!

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:30.820
This is the home of the Nebula Cup, Calmwind!

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.510
R-Right...

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:40.720
T-That takes care of the Hakuoh Academy entry.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.220
T-Thanks...

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:47.140
Everyone, we're leaving.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.770
Okay.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:52.940
It's true.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:53.770
Huh?

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.190
So they're the students from that school.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.980
Don't hide behind me.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.700
They finally came back.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.490
I'm amazed they did.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.700
What is all this?

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.570
Everyone's glaring at us.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:05.160
What an unpleasant greeting.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.330
I'm scared.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.910
I don't like this.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:08.910
Yeah, really.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.250
I'll ask what's up.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:20.430
Hey,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.840
I'd like to ask you something...

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.180
That's enough.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.430
You really worried me back there.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.020
So you're with the Sea of the Foreststar's team?

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.270
I'm helping them out.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.320
Not every team has as much top talent as yours.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.070
True, we had enough to go pirating after all.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.200
This isn't a joke.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.160
Do you understand your position here?

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.200
It's that incident, isn't it?

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.210
Oh, that's right!

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:56.530
The Hakuoh Academy Yacht Club received a five-year suspension from official races, didn't they?

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.130
They did?!

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:00.210
Huh?

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.880
Why did you not know that?!

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.720
That explains why we never received any invitations.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.350
But if it happened six years ago,

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.560
wouldn't you have been in middle school?

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:13.060
Oh, well...

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:17.480
Back then, some upperclassmen received
some unreleased race information.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.570
This course is so easy it's boring.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:21.360
Yeah.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.240
This won't satisfy the other teams either.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:32.830
So they asked me to rewrite the race data.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.040
You cracked their computers?

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.750
The race management must have been taken by surprise.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:44.010
On the day of the race, they discovered all
the course settings had been changed.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.010
And this was the result.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.220
"Named the 13th Tournament Nightmare.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.940
One hundred forty-two entrants, two finishers."

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.900
That must have been bad.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.820
And now, the cause of it all has returned.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:03.070
I didn't know it was such a big deal.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:03.740
I'm blushing.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:04.570
That's not a compliment!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.350
So no one likes us?

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.760
More accurately, everyone will be out to get you.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.080
J-Jeez...

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:15.210
And to think, we're even on the same planet as back then.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.090
Target is not with the rest of the group.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.340
I'll keep an eye out.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.550
That's...

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.430
There you are.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.730
Ai, you should get back to the ship and prepare.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:35.940
Yayoi, look!

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.190
A book of constellations?

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.230
Yeah.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:42.940
They only sell constellation books
on the planet you see them from!

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.650
Twenty minutes until the race begins.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.660
All teams, please submit your registration.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.990
That concludes the report from public relations.
Understood. Please finish within five minutes.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.240
We'll change from 3.5 to 4.5

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.660
Releasing partial GPS capabilities.
Understood. Please finish within five minutes.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.500
and await their instructions.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.660
Please re-confirm.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:58.580
Team 6 has deployed.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.750
The medics?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.750
They'll be ready in 27 seconds.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.840
Once it starts, get three more people there.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.340
Um...

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.720
Block 16, you're falling behind!
Get the observation probes in position.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.970
Progress is 97.3% complete.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:15.350
The Harold Lloyd Insurance Union
recommended us to provide security.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.520
I'm the captain of the Bentenmaru...

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.770
Low pressure is developing in the northern hemisphere.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.400
It's small enough to ignore.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.150
I'd like to discuss the security equipment...

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.740
I won't let these five years of work go to waste.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.700
I'm borrowing a dinghy, okay?

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.330
Just return it to its place when you're done.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.620
Okay, thanks!

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:41.290
Huh?

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.800
That couldn't have been...

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:51.180
They seemed too busy to talk.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:55.560
Even if it's for security purposes,
you don't need to fly personally, do you?

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.060
If the Bentenmaru can't descend into the atmosphere, we don't have a choice.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.480
It's a spaceship, after all.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.610
There's a limit to what you can see long range from orbit.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.900
Isn't it safer to watch from within the course?

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.610
Sure, but be careful.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.950
I just saw someone suspicious.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:12.990
Got it.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.280
Watch the Bentenmaru for me, okay?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:25.750
Curse you, Hakuoh Academy!

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:27.210
Chairwoman...

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.720
Um, about the pirate who just left...

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.970
What?!

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.940
I'm going to win. I'm going to win.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.690
I'm going to win. I'm going to win.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:52.700
One hundred eighty seconds until the race begins.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.030
Yayoi, hold on to this for me.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.030
Sure.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.330
Good luck.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:57.950
Thanks!

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.960
I wonder how the sky looks.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.880
It's hard to keep calm.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.190
Oh, yeah.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.480
Normally, I have everyone else.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:32.240
The starting gun will be fired by Gruier Serenity,
seventh princess of the Serenity royal family.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:43.410
Her younger sister Grunhilde will be taking part in the race,

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:48.340
and she says she's greatly looking forward to it.
So that's why I didn't see her.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:49.920
Princess, whenever you're ready.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.890
Course route has been released.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.480
It's finally here!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:08.610
A dinghy's propellant isn't nearly enough for this, is it?

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.610
Without a good wind, you'll be out for sure.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.330
Three...

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.330
Two...

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.330
One...

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:25.660
Start!

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.220
I'm on my way, okay?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:46.730
This is my responsibility!

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.900
Hakuoh Academy...

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.490
What are you plotting now?

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.640
Okay.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:26.890
What?

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.440
That's dangerous.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.530
I guess this really is a tournament.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.900
Everyone's so good.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.440
It'll be hard to keep up.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.320
Huh? From behind me?

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.330
You pirate, wait!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.420
W-Wait, was that the chairwoman?

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.420
Are you sure you can handle that speed?

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.670
I will stop your plans!

00:10:57.980 --> 00:10:59.130
Give up!

00:10:59.130 --> 00:10:59.720
Huh?

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.430
What? Wait!

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.190
What's going on?

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.710
The wind on this planet is strong!

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:42.930
Okay, found the checkpoint.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.940
Heavy noise on standard comms and radar.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.110
It's even affecting super-space.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.690
An EM storm from the system's main star.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.110
Incoming coronal mass ejection.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:11:59.690
It's strong!

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.240
A solar flare?

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.200
Now of all times?

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.700
Jeez, cut it out!

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.620
She isn't doing anything yet.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:11.910
Does she have an accomplice?

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:18.670
What is this?

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:22.930
No good.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:24.680
The EM storm's knocking it offline.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:26.010
How is it there?

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:26.890
Pretty...

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:27.180
Huh?

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.680
The aurora is so beautiful!

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.520
Does this planet have auroras?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.190
You didn't know?

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.900
I just swapped the data the upperclassman gave me.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.440
But you can't fly right in all this.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:40.950
Ai...

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:48.660
What is this?

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:49.540
What's happening?

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.080
What are you saying?

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:54.540
This is the planet's other face.

00:12:54.820 --> 00:13:00.050
I recreated the course Hakuoh Academy set six years ago!

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.260
Checkpoint 1 cleared.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:12.270
Everyone's amazing.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:16.730
Our upperclassmen have trained us hard over the past five years

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:21.280
so that we could repay the humiliation they suffered.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:25.530
Everyone got so frustrated they ended up raising the level of the tournament?

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.280
That's why everyone's so good.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.790
But I won't let you interfere anymore!

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.290
I said I don't know what you're talking about!

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.120
Stop.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:37.750
Something's there!

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.730
These guys must be the Bisque Company.

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:45.720
They got the drop on us!

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:47.630
You're late, Kane!

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:49.850
It's an ambush. The captain's in danger!

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.930
So which one is Kato Marika?

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.730
Can't tell. Get them all!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.610
Gunfire? Pirates?

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:01.730
Is Hakuoh behind this?

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:02.820
No!

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.360
They're attacking me too!

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:05.240
Everyone, run!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:06.490
You've gotta run too, Captain.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.950
They're after you.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.660
A lot of people are jealous of your pirate license.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:16.540
They're firing randomly too.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.920
They don't know which dinghy you're in!

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:19.920
Get out of there now!

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.310
Don't be stupid!

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.300
Marika!

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.100
Chiaki, take care of the rest!

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.310
Don't get shot down.

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:36.980
I'll do my best!

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.310
I'll lead you away.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:38.980
Follow me.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.230
If they're after me...

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.230
I'm right here!

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:48.400
What?

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.860
Isn't this their insignia?

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:51.740
What?

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.700
She's messing with us.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:58.910
That's Kato Marika.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:14:59.870
Shoot her down.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.050
What?

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:11.300
She's endangering herself to distract them?

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.930
Hakuoh really isn't behind this?

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:23.940
This isn't like the simulations at all!

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.070
It's harder than I expected.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.000
I'm sorry.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.250
I didn't think you'd go so far to protect the race!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:43.920
I'll help as best I can!

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:44.630
Wait! Stay back! It's dangerous!

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:48.090
First, to apologize for our rudeness toward you...

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:51.680
I can't tell which one it is!

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.470
Shoot them both down!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.220
I get it! I get it!
And after appropriate measures are passed...

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:56.220
Chairwoman?!

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.650
If we can shoot her down...

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:13.610
Captain!

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:26.590
The Bentenmaru!

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:27.540
Get inside!

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:29.170
This is crazy, Kane.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.050
The ship isn't made to fly in an atmosphere!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.720
Emergency output at 132%!

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.340
Sub-thrusters are overheating!

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:36.350
We won't last fifteen minutes!

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.850
Captain, please hurry.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:40.600
The Bentenmaru?

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:42.270
No one mentioned this.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:43.100
They're insane.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:46.440
Descending this far with just a spaceship...

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.860
No, we might be able to win this.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:52.360
A spaceship within the atmosphere is like a fish out of water.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:53.360
Follow me.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:55.360
Marika...

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.570
Hey! Stay on course!

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:58.620
Keep up!

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:01.580
You're all insane.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:02.660
Captain!

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.750
You never mentioned being able to fly in atmosphere!

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.250
We're not flying...

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:07.460
We're falling with style!

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:08.500
But you saved me!

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.250
Thanks, everyone.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.550
Okay, let's finish them.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:14.260
Roger.

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.010
We can do this.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:20.310
Space pirates can't fight within a planet's atmosphere!

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.020
What's hitting us?

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.230
Machine guns.

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:24.560
Small-caliber bullets.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.190
Old school.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.690
But this is a spaceship.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.820
Colliding with debris comes with the job.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:31.570
Counterattack! Prepare main cannon!

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:32.530
We can't.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.740
The air is too thick.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:40.450
If we fire a high-output energy weapon like that,
the air will expand and explode right in front of us.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.080
Then...

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.540
We've lost a piece of the #2 antenna plate!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.080
Not good... Those things pack a punch.

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.080
If they hit the thrusters, we'll go down!

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.170
This is bad.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:51.840
What do we do?

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.340
What to do...

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:56.590
Got it!

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:57.680
Ah, we'll use <i>that</i>.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:17:59.760
Oh, yeah!

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:02.100
Right, we could even use it at this close range.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.220
Thing from before?
What thing from before?

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.350
Come on, don't be silly.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:07.850
Schnitzer, get ready!

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:08.850
Already on it.

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.480
W-Wait...

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.360
I'm not gonna be able to get them aligned.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:15.610
We're using all our thrusters inside the atmosphere.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:17.610
We can't turn quickly!

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.870
And even if we could, they're faster, so we can't aim.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:22.870
And no one's stupid enough to fly right in front of us!

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:27.710
It's no good.

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:28.870
We're gonna lose a thruster!

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:32.210
Attention, Bentenmaru.

